bindings-common
===============

Native C/C++ library shared by the COMPSs language bindings (Python, C/C++,
etc.). It provides the glue between the bindings and the COMPSs Java runtime
and exposes a uniform interface over the JNI, named-pipe, and UNIX-socket
transports.

Layout
------

  src/                  Library sources (libbindings_common).
  tests/                Unit tests.
    harness/            Test doubles for the runtime API and transports.
    internal/           Test-only headers and the in-tree microtest framework.
    stubs/              Lightweight header stubs used by the tests.
  install_common        Helper script used by the parent build to install the
                        library into a target prefix.
  autogen.sh            Regenerates the Autotools build system.
  clean.sh              Removes generated Autotools artefacts.

Requirements
------------

  - GNU Autotools (autoconf, automake, libtool)
  - A C++11 compiler (g++ recommended)
  - JDK with JNI headers; JAVA_HOME must point at it
  - pthread (linked from the test binary)

The unit tests no longer depend on googletest, gmock, or cmake. The only
extra runtime requirement beyond what the library itself needs is pthread.

Build
-----

From this directory:

    ./autogen.sh
    ./configure
    make

The shared library is produced at src/.libs/libbindings_common.so. Use the
top-level COMPSs build (or install_common) to install it into the runtime
layout consumed by the bindings.

To start from a pristine tree (removes configure, Makefiles, m4, etc.):

    ./clean.sh

Running the tests
-----------------

The unit tests live under tests/ and are wired into the standard Autotools
"check" target. After configuring and building the library:

    make check

This builds the test binary (linking against libbindings_common, the test
harness library, and the in-tree microtest framework) and runs it through
the Autotools test driver. Per-test logs are written to tests/test-suite.log
and tests/test_gs_compss.log; on failure those files contain the full output.

The driver prints gtest-compatible status lines (`[ RUN ] / [ OK ] / [ FAILED ]`)
so existing CI parsing keeps working.

Coverage instrumentation (--coverage) is enabled by default for the test
build, so .gcno/.gcda files are produced alongside the test objects.

Running a subset of tests
-------------------------

The test binary accepts a googletest-style glob filter, matched against the
full `Suite.Name` (plus `/param` for parameterized cases). `*` matches any
run of characters and `?` matches one, so patterns must cover the whole name
-- wrap a fragment in `*` to match anywhere:

    ./tests/test_gs_compss --filter='*BarrierGroup*'
    ./tests/test_gs_compss --filter='*/sockets'       # only the sockets variants
    ./tests/test_gs_compss --filter='CompssSocketsTest.*'

Several patterns can be separated with `:`, and a `-` introduces patterns to
exclude:

    ./tests/test_gs_compss --filter='*Barrier*:*Snapshot*'
    ./tests/test_gs_compss --filter='-*/sockets'      # everything but sockets

For backwards compatibility with prior googletest-based invocations,
`--gtest_filter=` is accepted as an alias and uses the same syntax.

A filter that selects no tests exits non-zero rather than reporting a vacuous
success, so a typo in a pattern fails loudly instead of passing silently.

Test layout
-----------

  tests/test_gs_compss.cc
        Main suite. Drives the public GS_* runtime API through a polymorphic
        TransportHarness/RuntimeApi abstraction (in tests/harness/) and runs
        every parameterized case against both the pipes and sockets
        transports. Verifies wire-format output and response parsing.

  tests/test_compss_sockets.cc
        White-box test for the UNIX-socket transport's connect-on-ready and
        retry-until-server-available behaviour. Reaches the internal entry
        points via tests/internal/compss_sockets_test_api.h, which keeps
        these symbols out of the shipped public header.

  tests/internal/microtest.{h,cc}, microtest_main.cc
        In-tree unit-test framework. ~330 lines total. Provides
        TEST/TEST_P, EXPECT_*/ASSERT_*, a substring filter and a simple
        registry. Replaces googletest. See the file headers for the
        public surface.

  tests/internal/gs_test_reset.cc
        Test-only translation unit that resets the cached workflow in
        GS_compss.cc between parameterized cases so tests stay independent
        when the parameterized suite switches transports. Externs the
        relevant globals from src/GS_compss.cc rather than adding a hook
        to production source.

Environment overrides honoured by the test build:

    COMPSS_BINDINGS_DEBUG=1   Set automatically by AM_TESTS_ENVIRONMENT so
                              that debug_printf branches are exercised.

To re-run the tests after editing sources, just run `make check` again — the
library and test binary are rebuilt incrementally.
